    "helpful_mechanics": "Long Day reduces exposure to darkness, and pausing while I think allows careful inspection. Contextual Space actions simplify repeated gathering and chopping. Basic tools, torches, campfires, traps, and cooked or raw foraged food are cheap, while common resources support steady early scoring. Beefalo can potentially be shaved at night, and armor plus a spear makes necessary combat safer.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Hunger, darkness, and hostile creatures punish indecision, and survival progress is lost on death rather than pooled. Procedural world layout can separate rocks, gold, reeds, spiders, pigs, and beefalo. Limited inventory space, recipe prototyping, exact mouse interactions, random combat drops, and crock-pot cooking all add execution risk within the three-hour cap."
